From 9a465860887c839b6cd4772be515439af5365c12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 15:21:12 +0000
Subject: wifi: mt76: mt7915: unregister thermal cooling device on hwmon
 failure

From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

[ Upstream commit b8286bc7fe520e7117e7b6e1a1fd4c0df439aa3a ]

mt7915_thermal_init() registered the thermal cooling device and its sysfs
link, then returned the hwmon registration error without undoing them.
The cooling device (not devm-managed) and the link then leaked, and its
callbacks referenced the freed phy. Unregister the cooling device before
returning the error.

Fixes: 0ae3ff568451 ("mt76: mt7915: fix hwmon temp sensor mem use-after-free")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
[ sashal: Added mt7915_unregister_thermal(phy) to the existing IS_ERR(hwmon) check, since the surrounding throttle_temp initialisation meant the upstream return lines had no context to match. ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7915/init.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7915/init.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7915/init.c
index cd9bf39861158..cbe3780474249 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7915/init.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7915/init.c
@@ -194,8 +194,10 @@ static int mt7915_thermal_init(struct mt7915_phy *phy)
 
 	hwmon = devm_hwmon_device_register_with_groups(&wiphy->dev, name, phy,
 						       mt7915_hwmon_groups);
-	if (IS_ERR(hwmon))
+	if (IS_ERR(hwmon)) {
+		mt7915_unregister_thermal(phy);
 		return PTR_ERR(hwmon);
+	}
 
 	/* initialize critical/maximum high temperature */
 	phy->throttle_temp[0] = 110;
-- 
